# Repo geography map

Orientation for placing a first contribution. There is no equivalent overview under `docs/` (only build/security docs). Per-area implementation detail lives in `.agents/skills/<area>/SKILL.md`.

## Version management

- Never hardcode package versions in `.csproj` files.
- Central versions: `eng/Versions.props` (version variables) + root `Directory.Packages.props` (central package versions; imports `eng/Versions.props`).
- `test/Directory.Packages.props` exists for out-of-tree / test-specific package pins.

## Source dependency direction (`src/`)

Arrows mean "depends on" (ProjectReference). Leaf projects have no in-repo project deps.

```
EFCore.Abstractions          # attributes/APIs usable without pulling in EF Core
EFCore.Analyzers            # Roslyn analyzers (shipped with EFCore)
Microsoft.Data.Sqlite.Core  # ADO.NET SQLite provider (no native binary)

EFCore ──► Abstractions, Analyzers
  ├─ EFCore.InMemory
  ├─ EFCore.Proxies
  ├─ EFCore.Cosmos                    # non-relational provider
  └─ EFCore.Relational
       ├─ EFCore.SqlServer
       │    ├─ EFCore.SqlServer.NTS          # NetTopologySuite
       │    └─ EFCore.SqlServer.HierarchyId  # also ► SqlServer.Abstractions
       ├─ EFCore.Sqlite.Core ──► Relational, Microsoft.Data.Sqlite.Core
       │    ├─ EFCore.Sqlite                 # meta: Core + native binary
       │    └─ EFCore.Sqlite.NTS
       └─ EFCore.Design                      # migrations + scaffolding

Microsoft.Data.Sqlite ──► Microsoft.Data.Sqlite.Core   # meta: Core + native binary
EFCore.SqlServer.Abstractions                           # HierarchyId types without full provider

Tooling (wrap shared `ef` exe; `ef` itself is not packed):
  ef ◄── dotnet-ef | EFCore.Tools (PMC) | EFCore.Tasks (MSBuild)
EFCore.Templates   # T4 scaffolding templates (standalone)

src/Shared/        # compile-linked helpers (Check, extensions) — not a project
```

| Project | Role |
|---------|------|
| `EFCore` | Core ORM: model, LINQ, change tracking, `SaveChanges` |
| `EFCore.Relational` | Shared ADO.NET relational layer (SQL gen, migrations infra, updates) |
| `EFCore.SqlServer` / `Sqlite*` / `Cosmos` / `InMemory` | Database providers |
| `EFCore.Design` | Design-time: migrations, scaffolding |
| `EFCore.Proxies` | Lazy-loading / change-tracking proxies |
| `Microsoft.Data.Sqlite*` | ADO.NET SQLite (usable without EF); EF Sqlite provider builds on Core |
| `dotnet-ef` / `EFCore.Tools` / `EFCore.Tasks` / `ef` | CLI / PMC / MSBuild tooling |

**Where to edit:** provider-specific SQL/behavior → that provider project; shared relational → `EFCore.Relational`; core LINQ/tracking/model → `EFCore`; migrations/scaffold UX → `EFCore.Design` (+ tooling projects for CLI surface).

## Test layout (`test/`)

Specification tests define *what* to assert; provider functional tests inherit and assert *how* (e.g. SQL). See `.agents/skills/testing/SKILL.md` before adding tests.

```
EFCore.Specification.Tests          # abstract, provider-agnostic
  ├─ *.FunctionalTests              # InMemory, Cosmos (non-relational)
  └─ Relational.Specification.Tests
       └─ {SqlServer,Sqlite}.FunctionalTests   # SQL baselines live here

Unit / isolated:  EFCore.Tests, Relational.Tests, {Provider}.Tests
Design / tooling: EFCore.Design.Tests, ef.Tests, dotnet-ef.Tests, Analyzers.Tests
ADO.NET:          Microsoft.Data.Sqlite*.Tests
Surface / AOT:    ApiBaseline.Tests, TrimmingTests, NativeAotTests
Integration:      AspNet.*, OData, CrossStore, FSharp, VisualBasic
```

**First-contribution placement:** bug in core behavior → unit test under `EFCore.Tests` (or `Relational.Tests`); LINQ/query contract → add/override in Specification + every relevant `*.FunctionalTests` provider; provider SQL → that provider's FunctionalTests (+ baselines).

## Related paths (not packages)

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `eng/` | Arcade build, `Versions.props`, Helix, ApiChief |
| `docs/` | Build/run instructions, security — not architecture |
| `.agents/skills/` | Deep area guides (query, migrations, model-building, …) |
